  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (1S,2S)-1-Phenyl-1,2-propanediol and Tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 10B, mediated through different target entities. The compound is linked to Sodium/potassium-transporting ATPase subunit alpha-1 and Potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, both of which are targets of corticosterone and perforamone B, respectively. These targets are all involved in signaling pathways that ultimately influence the activity of Tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 10B. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with the strongest evidence coming from the connection to Potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which is directly targeted by perforamone B. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a possible functional link between the compound and the receptor, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated."
